save it is to basically,

00:20:26.158 --> 00:20:27.626
destroy all industry.

00:20:27.626 --> 00:20:28.827
And even if that happens,

00:20:28.827 --> 00:20:30.028
we're still not going
to save it anyway,

00:20:30.028 --> 00:20:31.530 align:start size:84% position:16%
but we should still
do it for some,

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:32.564
you know, dubious purpose.

00:20:32.564 --> 00:20:35.067
So the goalposts keep changing

00:20:35.067 --> 00:20:37.102
and I think I've mentioned
this previously on the show,

00:20:37.102 --> 00:20:38.604
I know I've spoken of it before,

00:20:38.604 --> 00:20:41.640 align:start size:97% position:3%
this goes back to the
early days of progressivism

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:45.077 align:start position:0%
and Woodrow Wilson, because
one of the things that happened

00:20:45.077 --> 00:20:48.447
during the Great War was
this the big, if I can,

00:20:48.447 --> 00:20:50.782 align:start size:84% position:16%
pardon my French,
progressive wet dream,

00:20:50.782 --> 00:20:54.253
which is we're going to have
Washington as this super state

00:20:54.253 --> 00:20:57.789
governing every single
aspect of our country,

00:20:57.789 --> 00:20:59.825
of our economy, of our culture.

00:20:59.825 --> 00:21:01.960
Now they had an excuse,
it was the Great War.

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:05.430
This is, you know, world
war, everyone's involved

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:08.667 align:start size:84% position:16%
but this was a great
dress rehearsal

00:21:08.667 --> 00:21:10.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the Great
Depression, the New Deal,

00:21:10.636 --> 00:21:13.205
because they can say,
look, 15 years ago

00:21:13.205 --> 00:21:14.673
